<title>MOLDOVA: MOLDOVAN FOREIGN TRADE DEFICIT WIDENS TO $187 MLN.</title>
<headline>MOLDOVAN FOREIGN TRADE DEFICIT WIDENS TO $187 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moldova's foreign trade deficit</p>
<p>widened to $187 million in January-August of this year from $24</p>
<p>million in the same period last year, a report from the State</p>
<p>Statistics Department said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said that imports in the first eight months of this year</p>
<p>grew by 42 percent to $694 million, while exports increased by</p>
<p>23 percent to $507 million.</p>
<p>Countries of the Commonwealth of Independent States</p>
<p>accounted for 70 percent of Moldovan exports and 61 percent of</p>
<p>imports. Russia alone accounted for 55 percent of exports and 28</p>
<p>percent of imports.</p>
<p>    MOLDOVAN FOREIGN TRADE	  Jan-Aug 1996     Jan-Aug 1995</p>
<p>(in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>    Exports				  507		415</p>
<p>    Imports				  694		439</p>
<p>    Balance				 -187		-24  REUTER</p>
</text>
